@* 2026-10-17: moved onto FeatureDemoLayout (one-example-plus-code push, tracker section 6). Same grid, data and aggregates, with
   three corrections: ShowGroupCount dropped because the Count aggregate's caption template already prints "(n items)", so every
   caption showed the count twice; the internal catalog name left the intro; "default sorts" left the intro because the page sets
   none. Two library behaviours shape the copy (logged in SC-253): a group footer prints only the first aggregate defined for a
   column, so the Count footer template never shows; and the caption aggregates' pill styling is scoped CSS that never matches the
   spans built in GridControl.razor.cs, so they run together, which the page CSS works around through the .catalog wrapper.
   2026-10-18: vocabulary written from GridControl.razor.cs (grouping parameters, AddGroup/RemoveGroup/ClearAllGroupsAsync, the public
   group methods, ComputeAggregates, FormatAggregateValue, the caption and footer renderers), GridControl.AdvancedFeatures.cs,
   GridColumn.cs, GridModels.cs (AggregateRow, AggregateColumn, GroupEventArgs), GridControlEvents.cs and GridEnums.cs; rows checked with
   scratchpad/vocabcheck.py. Declared-but-unused members are named as such; library notes in SC-253.
   2026-10-20 (meeting point 2): the unlisted Assembly and Vendor prices pages fold in here. Vendor prices repeated this page's
   configuration (grouped by one column, average and count in captions and footers) on other data, so it is gone; Assembly becomes
   the second example, because it shows the one thing the catalog does not: sums in the grid footer with no initial grouping. Both
   old routes now open this page. *@

<PageTitle>Grouping &amp; totals — FlexCore Showcase</PageTitle>

<FeatureDemoLayout Title="Grouping &amp; totals" Category="Data Grid" CategoryHref="demo/grid" ControlName="GridControl"
                   Tagline="Group rows by a column, with averages, counts and sums in the group captions, group footers and the grid footer."
                   SourcePath="Grid/GridControl.razor.cs;Grid/GridModels.cs;Grid/GridControlEvents.cs;Grid/GridEnums.cs">
    <Overview>
        <p>
            <code>GroupColumns</code> opens the grid already grouped; with <code>AllowGrouping</code> the user regroups by dragging a header
            into the bar above the grid. <code>AggregateRows</code> lists what to compute per group: each <code>AggregateColumn</code> names a
            field, an <code>AggregateType</code> and a format, and its <code>GroupCaptionTemplate</code> and <code>GroupFooterTemplate</code>
            decide where the value is printed and how; <code>ShowInFooter</code> prints the same values once more under the whole grid.
            <code>ShowSearchBar</code> adds a search box to the grid toolbar.
        </p>
    </Overview>

    <Examples>
        <DemoExample Id="catalog" Title="Item catalog grouped by category" RazorCode="@Code.Catalog" CSharpCode="@Code.CatalogCs">
            <Description><p>A cost-item catalog: material, labor, subcontract, equipment and overhead lines keyed by phase, each with a default cost and an Active flag. It opens grouped by <strong>Category</strong>; drag <strong>Phase</strong> into the bar to regroup. Each caption shows the average default cost and the item count; each footer repeats the average. Sort <strong>Default $</strong> descending for the priciest items, filter <strong>Active</strong> for the inactive ones, or type in the search box.</p></Description>
            <Demo>
                <div class="catalog">
                <GridControl TValue="CatalogItem"
                             DataSource="@_items"
                             AllowSelection="true"
                             AllowSorting="true"
                             AllowFiltering="true"
                             AllowGrouping="true"
                             AllowResizing="true"
                             AllowColumnReorder="true"
                             EnableHover="true"
                             ShowSearchBar="true"
                             Height="520px"
                             GroupColumns="@_groupColumns"
                             AggregateRows="_aggregates">
                    <GridColumnsBase>
                        <GridColumn Field="@nameof(CatalogItem.ItemId)"      HeaderText="Item ID"     Width="110px" />
                        <GridColumn Field="@nameof(CatalogItem.Description)" HeaderText="Description" Width="260px" />
                        <GridColumn Field="@nameof(CatalogItem.Phase)"       HeaderText="Phase"       Width="160px" />
                        <GridColumn Field="@nameof(CatalogItem.Category)"    HeaderText="Category"    Width="160px" />
                        <GridColumn Field="@nameof(CatalogItem.UOM)"         HeaderText="UOM"         Width="70px" />
                        <GridColumn Field="@nameof(CatalogItem.DefaultCost)" HeaderText="Default $"   Width="120px"
                                    Type="ColumnType.Number" Format="C2" TextAlign="TextAlign.Right" />
                        <GridColumn Field="@nameof(CatalogItem.IsActive)"    HeaderText="Active"      Width="80px"
                                    Type="ColumnType.Boolean" TextAlign="TextAlign.Center" />
                    </GridColumnsBase>
                </GridControl>
                </div>
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>
        <DemoExample Id="assembly" Title="Line items with sums in the footer, grouped on demand" RazorCode="@Code.Assembly" CSharpCode="@Code.AssemblyCs">
            <Description><p>Sixty assembly lines, not grouped to start with. The grid footer sums <code>Qty</code> and <code>Total</code>; drag <strong>PO Index</strong> or <strong>Vendor</strong> into the bar above the grid and every group gets the same sums in its footer, while the grid footer keeps the overall total. <code>ShowInGroupFooter</code> and <code>ShowInFooter</code> are both on; there is no caption aggregate here.</p></Description>
            <Demo>
                <div class="catalog">
                <GridControl TValue="AssemblyItem"
                             DataSource="@_lines"
                             AllowSelection="true"
                             AllowSorting="true"
                             AllowFiltering="true"
                             AllowGrouping="true"
                             AllowResizing="true"
                             AllowColumnReorder="true"
                             ShowSearchBar="true"
                             Height="420px"
                             AggregateRows="_sums">
                    <GridColumnsBase>
                        <GridColumn Field="@nameof(AssemblyItem.PriceLevel)"  HeaderText="Price Level" Width="150px" />
                        <GridColumn Field="@nameof(AssemblyItem.Vendor)"      HeaderText="Vendor"      Width="170px" />
                        <GridColumn Field="@nameof(AssemblyItem.POIndex)"     HeaderText="PO Index"    Width="110px" />
                        <GridColumn Field="@nameof(AssemblyItem.Description)" HeaderText="Description" Width="230px" />
                        <GridColumn Field="@nameof(AssemblyItem.Qty)"         HeaderText="Qty"         Width="80px"
                                    Type="ColumnType.Number" Format="N0" TextAlign="TextAlign.Right" />
                        <GridColumn Field="@nameof(AssemblyItem.UOM)"         HeaderText="UOM"         Width="70px" />
                        <GridColumn Field="@nameof(AssemblyItem.Price)"       HeaderText="Unit Price"  Width="110px"
                                    Type="ColumnType.Number" Format="C2" TextAlign="TextAlign.Right" />
                        <GridColumn Field="@nameof(AssemblyItem.Total)"       HeaderText="Total"       Width="120px"
                                    Type="ColumnType.Number" Format="C2" TextAlign="TextAlign.Right" />
                    </GridColumnsBase>
                </GridControl>
                </div>
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>
    </Examples>

    <Vocabulary>
        <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="GridControl grouping parameters" Rows="Vocab.Grid" />
        <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="GridColumn" Rows="Vocab.Column" />
        <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Properties" Title="AggregateRow" Rows="Vocab.Row" />
        <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Properties" Title="AggregateColumn" Rows="Vocab.Agg" />
        <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Events" Title="GridControlEvents, grouping" Rows="Vocab.Events" />
        <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Methods" Title="Grouping methods" Rows="Vocab.Methods" />
        <p>
            <code>AggregateType</code> is <code>Sum</code>, <code>Average</code>, <code>Count</code>, <code>Min</code> or <code>Max</code>. Values are
            read as doubles: numeric properties directly, anything else through a parse of its text. <code>Count</code> therefore counts the
            values that parse as numbers, so on a text or boolean column it prints nothing; count a numeric column instead, as this page does.
            A group footer and the grid footer print one value per column, the first <code>AggregateColumn</code> for that field; a caption
            prints every value of every caption row.
        </p>
    </Vocabulary>

    <Related>
        <ul>
            <li><a href="demo/grid">Grid overview</a>: the core flags on a small list.</li>
            <li><a href="demo/pivot">Pivot tables</a>: totals as a cross-tab instead of groups.</li>
            <li><a href="demo/grid/provider-enterprise">On-demand loading</a>: the same captions and footers, with the values supplied by a provider.</li>
        </ul>
    </Related>
</FeatureDemoLayout>

@code {
    private List<CatalogItem> _items = DemoData.GenerateItemCatalog();

    private List<string> _groupColumns = new() { nameof(CatalogItem.Category) };

    private List<AggregateRow> _aggregates = new()
    {
        new AggregateRow
        {
            ShowInGroupCaption = true,
            ShowInGroupFooter = true,
            Columns = new()
            {
                new AggregateColumn { Field = nameof(CatalogItem.DefaultCost), Type = AggregateType.Average, Format = "C2",
                    GroupCaptionTemplate = "avg {value}", GroupFooterTemplate = "Avg {value}" },
                new AggregateColumn { Field = nameof(CatalogItem.DefaultCost), Type = AggregateType.Count,
                    GroupCaptionTemplate = "({value} items)", GroupFooterTemplate = "{value} items" },
            }
        }
    };

    // Assembly lines (moved here from the Assembly page, 2026-10-20): sums in group footers and the grid footer, no initial group.
    private List<AssemblyItem> _lines = DemoData.GenerateAssemblyItems(60);

    private List<AggregateRow> _sums = new()
    {
        new AggregateRow
        {
            ShowInGroupFooter = true,
            ShowInFooter = true,
            Columns = new()
            {
                new AggregateColumn { Field = nameof(AssemblyItem.Qty),   Type = AggregateType.Sum, Format = "N0", FooterTemplate = "Σ {value}", GroupFooterTemplate = "Σ {value}" },
                new AggregateColumn { Field = nameof(AssemblyItem.Total), Type = AggregateType.Sum, Format = "C2", FooterTemplate = "Σ {value}", GroupFooterTemplate = "Σ {value}" },
            }
        }
    };

